  <prompt>
    Flagship gate G — the final judgment gate. Verify that ALL 8 spec Success Criteria are GREEN and record
    the verdict in `notes/flagship-gate-decision.md`. Map EACH criterion to its verifying artifact:
    (1) Byte-preserving → the corpus byte-diff harness run (034/061).
    (2) Placement determinism → corpus + code audit + seam tests (zero write-path text-search).
    (3) AI drift-proof → the concurrent-edit ProseMirror test (042) + the CIPO UAT (062).
    (4) Concurrency → the stale-base re-anchor + 423 seam slices (054) + the CIPO UAT (062).
    (5) Structural edits → the split/merge/insert/delete corpus round-trip (031/034).
    (6) Word-native output → the CIPO UAT open-in-Word-for-web (062).
    (7) Hard-replace complete → the grep-audit (060) + the publish-size report (061) + CI green.
    (8) Phase-0-gate-passed-before-cutover → the commit/PR ordering showing 006 green PRIOR to any old-path
        deletion (023/032/060).
    Give each criterion a GREEN or RED verdict citing the exact artifact. Project completion is authorized
    ONLY if all 8 are GREEN. If ANY criterion is RED, BLOCK project completion (task 090) and escalate per
    root §6. This is a GATE task — no new surface, no `&lt;justification&gt;`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior engineer / release gatekeeper performing the final go/no-go on a mission-critical hard-replace.
    Fluent in the R4 spec Success Criteria, the evidence artifacts each depends on, and the root §6/§6.5
    escalation protocol. Renders a defensible GREEN/RED verdict that authorizes or blocks project completion.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A recorded flagship-gate decision (`notes/flagship-gate-decision.md`) mapping each of the 8 spec Success
    Criteria to its verifying artifact (harness run, seam slice, UAT, grep, publish report) with a GREEN or
    RED verdict per criterion. Project completion (task 090) is authorized ONLY on an all-green verdict; any
    red criterion blocks completion and is escalated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §10 (Success Criteria — graduation) and spec §Success Criteria (the 8 criteria, verbatim):
      1 byte-preserving, 2 placement determinism, 3 AI drift-proof, 4 concurrency, 5 structural edits,
      6 Word-native output, 7 hard-replace complete, 8 Phase-0-gate-passed-before-cutover. This is the
      terminal quality gate before wrap-up (090). It does not produce code — it audits the accumulated
      evidence from the whole project (Phase 0 gate 006, patch-engine corpus proof 034, corpus re-run 061,
      structural ops 031, AI concurrent-edit test 042, concurrency seam slices 054, hard-replace grep 060,
      CIPO UAT 062) and renders a verdict. The commit/PR ordering evidence for criterion 8 (006 green before
      any deletion in 023/032/060) is verifiable from git history.
    </background>
